title The build that lived in a comment -- two Comlink witnesses prove nothing on a clone, and a meter now counts the other 46
prompt Open as SILENCE under the INNER LOOP Standing block -- roster cold then hot, reds first as standfast, QA on touch, council rota row N mod 5, prose witnesses on prose sends, stamp-and-name, ASCII-first, READ SCOPE -- then pick up the running thread and take the infrastructure lane.
think ListAgents at the open named one peer, grain-96, interactive, started an hour before. Nothing of mine moved a file until the roster had closed, and the peer landed the tools/fixtures letter fold mid-run -- HEAD went e2e5ee013 to e33a8cc48 and context/GAUGE_STYLE.md was repointed under me. My first cold roster was bound to refuse under tree_moved from that moment, so I killed it and re-opened on tools/fixtures/s/standing_equipment_run.sh, the runner's own new path.
think The rota computed row 3. N is git rev-list --count HEAD at 3658, and 3658 mod 5 is 3. My previous Silence lap read row 0, so this advances rather than repeats and no hand advance was owed. Water, Venus, care and flow, sense of taste -- read up close, run the actual witness. Three of my last five laps have now read row 3, which is the commit-counted N the seed itself already documents as delivering the promise on about half of transitions.
think The lane's charter, active-designing/20260827-174816, names two defects it booked rather than fixed. Both were already repaired by other hands -- the dual-bind probe path and the Constel naming split -- so the charter's plan is closed except the socket (Keaton's word) and the deep debride (gate %5). The lane needed a finding of its own.
think witness_reach_scan.sh answered it: Mantra holds 15 unreached witnesses, Comlink 4, and all four Comlink ones are unheard -- named by no runner anywhere in the tree, not the roster, not a suite, not another witness. Reading those four is what found the real fault.
think tools/co/comlink_handshake_turn_witness.rish and comlink_turn_route_witness.rish each carry `# Build first:  rye build ... -femit-bin=comlink/bin/...` in the header and then `run ["comlink/bin/handshake-turn" "selftest"]`. comlink/bin/ is gitignored at .gitignore:185, so a clone carries no binary; a comment builds nothing. Both read GREEN on this bench only because an August lap left binaries behind. Their sibling comlink_topology_witness.rish:19 already carries the build and its own comment records the same discovery -- one of three was repaired and nothing counted the other two.
think I proved the repair from the fresh-clone condition rather than from the bench's leftovers: moved comlink/bin/handshake-turn and turn-route to /tmp, ran both witnesses, watched each build its own binary and report GREEN, and re-ran the topology sibling to be sure I had broken nothing.
obs A class measured before it was believed, and the measurement closed one question and opened another. My first idea was a guard on dangling path literals inside tool sources -- 567 raw, 74 rooted at a real tracked room, and of my lane's six every single one was correct: three were ${pen}/ scratch the regex had stripped, two were deliberate `test ! -e` absence assertions in seva_rename_witness.rish, one was a resolver input. So that class does not support a gate, and saying so is the honest answer to the frame rather than building the loom anyway.
obs The class that did support one is narrower and exact: a witness invoking a path GIT ITSELF ignores, with no build for it in its own non-comment lines. 65 such pairs, 17 already self-built, 48 unbuilt across 37 witnesses; 14 of the 28 distinct artifacts are missing from this very bench right now, so those witnesses are red today on a machine that has been building for weeks. After the two Comlink repairs it reads 46 over 35, which is the seated ceiling.
obs My own red, caught by my own draft and worth writing down. Batching the scan for speed, I reached for `xargs -a`, a GNU flag this BSD bench refuses -- the pipeline died, every count read zero, and the scan printed verdict=ok. A guard reading nothing passes as readily as one reading everything, which is phantom_path_scan.sh's own sentence about this tree. The scan now refuses with verdict=extraction_empty when it holds witnesses and extracts not one invoked path, and the control proves that refusal.
obs The control caught a second fault of mine before it shipped. Case 7, which asserts the honest `sh -c` limit, planted a pen whose only invocation was the unread one -- so the scan correctly answered extraction_empty and the case read no. The pen now carries a second tracked invocation, and the comment says why, since a reader meeting that line deserves to know it was earned.
obs Speed was a design decision rather than a detail. The first working draft took 3m57s, quadratic in targets times runners. One awk over the whole witness population, one batched `git check-ignore --stdin`, and one collected pass of every build line in the tree bring it to 4.7s -- which is what let the roster row read `tier lap` instead of `cadence`. A check nobody can afford stops being a check, which is the fixed seat of the row I read today.
obs The ledger is genuinely full, and this is the card's named structural seat arriving as a fact. construction/REDS.md had 811 bytes of headroom and my row wanted 1,096. Four trims brought it to 807 and the pin now stands at 24,572 of 24,576 -- four bytes. reds_fold.sh refuses OPEN rows and every remaining row reads OPEN, so the next red cannot be booked in full without a seat Keaton holds. I said so on the card rather than trimming a fifth time.
obs Six roster reds, and sorting them by owner is the whole triage. readme_reach (broken_total=1229), foundations_link, reds_fold and geode_libraries are the aftermath of the peer's fixtures letter fold, landed while my roster ran; generated_page_freshness reads core.hooksPath as an absolute /Users/... path on this bench, which is an environment fact rather than a tree red; remember_git_nib was stale because peers landed five commits during the lap, and my own work commit repins it. None was mine to cross and none is routed around.
obs The tree moved twice under this lap -- tree_at_close=bac9ebeb5ce8 against the open, and five peer commits between my roster's start and its finish. A 35-minute cold roster on a checkout three hands write cannot close on a still tree, which is REDS %291's family rather than a new fault, and I name it here rather than booking it again.
obs Added at round close, after the rebase. My row booked %334 rather than %333, and the derived-spine law decided it rather than I did: `git fetch xy` before the push showed a peer had booked %333 at stamp 20260828.212447 -- eleven minutes before mine -- and landed it upstream inside construction/archive/REDS-the-witness-the-fold-left-behind-rows-333.md. A published number never moves and mine was unshared, so mine shifted. The same fetch found the ledger folded under me, which is why the rebase conflicted on four files; I took upstream's REDS.md whole and re-appended my row, kept every peer index row, and let the pre-commit hook regenerate the two derived pages. The pin reads 24,571 of 24,576 after the fold, so the full-ledger observation above stands with different numbers rather than being undone.
